  "goodToKnow": "Die Lesung is a public reading of an author from their own work, common in bookshops and at the Leipziger Buchmesse. It's also a reading in church (the Lesung from the Bible) and a stage in the legislative process: In the Bundestag, bills go through several readings (erste, zweite, dritte Lesung). The verb is lesen, but Vorlesung (university lecture) is a different event, so don't mix the two."
